    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st period",
        "score": "LA 1, BOS 0",
        "text": "Alex Laferriere, promoted to the Kings' top line, scored 31 seconds in, tapping in Adrian Kempe's feed after Jeremy Swayman stopped a Brandt Clarke point shot. With Pavel Zacha (upper body) out, Boston struggled early against Los Angeles' 1-3-1 neutral-zone trap."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd period",
        "score": "BOS 1, LA 1",
        "text": "David Pastrnak tied it 1–1 at 2:43, jumping on a puck Erik Gustafsson couldn't keep in the zone and firing a wrist shot from the right circle on the rush. It was his 289th even-strength goal, tying Phil Esposito for third in Bruins history."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd period",
        "score": "Final: BOS 4, LA 1",
        "text": "With 6:24 left, Anton Forsberg couldn't cover Morgan Geekie's shot from the left circle, Matthew Poitras knocked the loose puck to Marat Khusnutdinov, and he backhanded it into the open net for a 2–1 lead. Elias Lindholm (18:02) and JJ Peterka (19:42) added empty-net goals."
      }
    ],
